  "description": "The attack table: one row per attack, addressed by \"index\". Harry's rows come first (weapon number + 10 * input, the input being tap, hold, run and so on), then the other characters' attacks; those rows have a \"name\" scripts address them by (sh.entity.attack_number(\"StalkerLunge\") gives the row's index). Fields, as the game stores them: reach_q12 / reach_start_q12 (reach in Q12 metres, 4096 = 1 m), power (damage), shape (six raw bytes of the hit shape), knockback_q12 (Q12), keyframe_start / keyframe_length (the animation keyframes in which the attack hits), hit_type, hurt_sound (-1 = none), blood_splatter (effect strength). A weapon's own \"attacks\" in weapons/<Name>.json override its rows here. A mod changes it with a file of the same path in its own folder; objects are merged key by key, so the patch only needs the keys it changes.",
